# Frontend configuration.
#
# Vite INLINES these at BUILD time — they are not read at runtime. Change one
# and you must rebuild and redeploy; restarting the app does nothing. That
# catches people out, so it is worth knowing before the first deploy.

# Where the API lives. Leave it UNSET for local development: every request then
# uses a relative /api/… path and the dev server proxies it to the backend, so
# the browser sees one origin and CORS never enters into it.
#
# Set it when the frontend and the API are on different domains — which is
# exactly what Vercel + Railway is. No trailing slash needed; one is stripped.
# VITE_API_URL=https://clear-api.up.railway.app

# Which backend the LOCAL dev server proxies to. Only used by vite.config.ts,
# never shipped to the browser. Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
# CLEAR_API=http://127.0.0.1:8001
